#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6835da4f-0783-54f5-9112-499b793c7b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416492} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3b6071-447a-5e5b-955a-60e039ddb364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416494} {:answer/id #uuid "84a27511-2f73-51ad-9efc-512adfb8573b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416496} {:answer/id #uuid "f032cbc3-7ec5-5ffd-9b44-86c708965b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416501} {:answer/id #uuid "f2544fdb-11f6-5f6b-b648-844f55f4831f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d3b6071-447a-5e5b-955a-60e039ddb364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416494} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd07d7b1-6cdf-5103-98fc-8aa75014e305" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86b78d29-f123-58f2-82ad-24e8b4486f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-146471" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=0.6,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=1,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4899,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.8944,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.1+0\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1+0\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & +1\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =0.5-(0.6)(1) \\\\  & =-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.1}{0.4899\\cdot 0.8944} \\\\  & ≈0.23,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "671ca342-974b-595d-90ce-f2d135a933c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416491} {:answer/id #uuid "76b4ff69-0d3b-5cf8-8bc0-c37eb66140b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416493} {:answer/id #uuid "8305d7f0-359a-5672-84b3-d2451cec6023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416495} {:answer/id #uuid "92d2fd3c-8d02-57f3-80c7-ad19c8e18d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416498} {:answer/id #uuid "990379fa-9ca9-5e21-9b76-b06e960628cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92d2fd3c-8d02-57f3-80c7-ad19c8e18d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416498} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7baad12-38b1-5f0c-9519-c9cab1926772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "972ce393-9eba-55fd-8649-cb51968b297d" :question/math-academy-id "q-148368" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ | $0.7$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=0.3\\,\\text{E}[Y]=0.2,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4583,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.9798,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0.2+0\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & +1\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0.2+1\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & =-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =-0.1-(0.3)(0.2) \\\\  & =-0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.16}{0.4583\\cdot 0.9798} \\\\  & ≈-0.36,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0876eb83-57bd-5e84-8477-dc5d60ce323d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416488} {:answer/id #uuid "54445a12-3783-54c9-a829-54a3a211f3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416489} {:answer/id #uuid "59e0c0fc-3c74-57a4-869c-4fa2f31bf145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416490} {:answer/id #uuid "90d7f216-f436-5ba1-90e3-d380e7bb6856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416497} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c6d741-b8ea-5c6d-a797-e6668be9d1b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d7f216-f436-5ba1-90e3-d380e7bb6856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416497} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3019da1-a157-5528-94a6-85caf91d61fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "71621138-ed93-53b4-9ace-266f4a0d5dab" :question/math-academy-id "q-148377" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-4$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.16$ | $0.17$ | $0.19$ | $0.52$ |\n| $X=10$ | $0.15$ | $0.17$ | $0.16$ | $0.48$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.31$ | $0.34$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=4.8,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=-0.54,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈4.9960,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈2.4634,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.16+0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.17+0\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.19 \\\\  & +10\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.15+10\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.17+10\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.16 \\\\  & =-2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =-2.8-(4.8)(-0.54) \\\\  & =-0.208.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.208}{4.9960\\cdot 2.4634} \\\\  & ≈-0.02,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}]}
